**Finding: missing** (LOL-CAP, critical)

The agreement contains no limitation of liability at all. I confirmed this by scanning the full outline and reading both substantive articles (§§1–5 and §§6–10), plus targeted searches for "liability", "damages", "consequential", "indemnif" and "aggregate" — the only hits were the no-joint-venture language in 10.2 and the Termination Payment mechanic in 4.2. Neither Warranties (§9) nor General Provisions (§10) caps or excludes anything.

Per the planner hint, absence of any usable clause is treated as **missing** rather than deviation. I proposed a new §10.9 (inside surviving Section 10) at the **preferred** position:

- mutual cap at the greater of 12 months' fees paid or payable by the Company and USD 1,000,000;
- mutual exclusion of indirect/consequential damages;
- uncapped carve-outs for confidentiality, data protection/security, indemnification, gross negligence, wilful misconduct, fraud and IP infringement;
- Company's payment obligations under §§3 and 4.2 expressly not "damages" for cap purposes.

The fee basis is substantive here (30% of Net Sales under §3.1), so a fee-referenced cap is not illusory. The comment offers the fallback (straight 12-month fee cap with core carve-outs) if HDI resists the USD 1,000,000 floor. Redline validated `ok:true` and the finding is submitted.
